Local patch: ghidra-mcp 5.7.0 headless server cannot start
=========================================================

Upstream bug, reproducible on a clean build of commit e6c325e
("bump ghidra version & date in Dockerfile"), Ghidra 12.0.4, Java 21.

Symptom
-------
    Ghidra initialized in headless mode
    Failed to launch headless server: cannot add context to list
    java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: cannot add context to list
        at jdk.httpserver/sun.net.httpserver.ContextList.add(ContextList.java:37)
        at jdk.httpserver/sun.net.httpserver.ServerImpl.createContext(ServerImpl.java:307)
        at jdk.httpserver/sun.net.httpserver.HttpServerImpl.createContext(HttpServerImpl.java:74)
        at com.xebyte.headless.GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.safeContext(GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java:561)
        at com.xebyte.headless.GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.registerEndpoints(GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java:379)

The server aborts in registerEndpoints() and never binds its port, so nothing can
reach it and the MCP bridge has no backend.

Cause
-----
GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.registerEndpoints() registers endpoints in two passes:

  1. the annotation-scanned service endpoints, via AnnotationScanner over
     @McpTool-annotated methods, and
  2. its own manual "headless-specific" contexts.

Two paths occur in both passes:

    /create_folder   core/ProgramScriptService.java:588   (annotation)
                    GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java:379      (manual, headless)
    /delete_file     core/ProgramScriptService.java:621   (annotation)
                    GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java:394      (manual, headless)

com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer.createContext() throws IllegalArgumentException
when a context for the path already exists, so the second pass dies on the first
collision. The GUI plugin (GhidraMCPPlugin) registers a different manual set, which
is why this only reproduces in headless mode.

Note: `/list_methods` looks like a third collision but does not matter - the second
occurrence is inside a javadoc example in core/McpTool.java, not an annotation.

Fix
---
Track the bound paths and replace on a duplicate instead of throwing.

Last-registration-wins is the correct semantics here, not a workaround. The
service-side /create_folder and /delete_file both begin with
`PluginTool tool = getToolFromProvider();` and return
"requires GUI mode (PluginTool not available)" when it is null, which is always the
case headless. The manual headless handlers delegate to HeadlessManagementService,
which works headlessly. Because the manual contexts are registered after the
scanner, replacing leaves the handler that actually functions in place.

A plain `server.removeContext(path)` is not sufficient: HttpServerImpl throws
IllegalStateException when the path is not bound, which is the common case. Hence the
Set, so removeContext is only reached on a genuine duplicate.

Applied patch
-------------
    --- a/src/main/java/com/xebyte/headless/GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java
    +++ b/src/main/java/com/xebyte/headless/GhidraMCPHeadlessServer.java

    @@ field declarations
         private int registeredEndpointCount;
    +
    +    // Local patch: paths already bound to an HttpContext, so a duplicate
    +    // registration can replace rather than throw. See
    +    // .opencode/patches/ghidra-mcp-5.7.0-headless-duplicate-context.patch
    +    private final java.util.Set<String> registeredContexts =
    +            java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();

    @@ safeContext()
         private com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpContext safeContext(
                 String path, com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpHandler handler) {
    +        // Local patch: createContext() throws on a duplicate path. /create_folder and
    +        // /delete_file are registered by both the annotation scanner and the manual
    +        // headless set, which aborts startup. See
    +        // .opencode/patches/ghidra-mcp-5.7.0-headless-duplicate-context.patch
    +        if (!registeredContexts.add(path)) {
    +            // Already present: replace it. The later registration is the
    +            // headless-specific one and must win, because the service-side
    +            // /create_folder and /delete_file require a GUI PluginTool and would
    +            // otherwise answer "requires GUI mode".
    +            server.removeContext(path);
    +        }
             return server.createContext(path, exchange -> {

Verified
--------
    before:  Failed to launch headless server: cannot add context to list
    after :  Registered 202 REST API endpoints
             HTTP server started on 127.0.0.1:8089
             GhidraMCP Headless Server v5.7.0-headless running on port 8089
             GET /check_connection -> Connection OK - GhidraMCP Headless Server v5.7.0-headless
             GET /mcp/schema        -> 171 endpoints

Scope
-----
Applied to the vendored checkout at .tools/ghidra-mcp-src, which is gitignored and
is not part of the NSMB repository. This is not an NSMB change, is not committed
upstream, and does not touch the NSMB project. The installer
.opencode/bin/build-ghidra-runtime re-applies it when rebuilding.
